      {
        "": "",
        "Tapping this icon displays information about the Cannon, such as Level, Damage Per Second, Hitpoints, Range, Damage Type, and Targets.": "Tapping this icon begins upgrading the Cannon to the next level, if you have enough resources and a free Builder (or B.O.B ). When the Cannon is at maximum level, this icon is not shown."
      },
      {
        "": "",
        "Tapping this icon displays information about the Cannon, such as Level, Damage Per Second, Hitpoints, Range, Damage Type, and Targets.": "Tapping this icon instantly upgrades the Cannon to the next level, at the cost of one Hammer of Building if you have one. When the Cannon is at maximum level, or if the Town Hall requirements for the next level are not met, this icon is not shown."
      },
      {
        "": "",
        "Tapping this icon displays information about the Cannon, such as Level, Damage Per Second, Hitpoints, Range, Damage Type, and Targets.": "Tapping this icon, which is displayed only while an upgrade is in progress, instantly finishes that upgrade at the cost of the displayed number of Gems ."
      },
      {
        "": "",
        "Tapping this icon displays information about the Cannon, such as Level, Damage Per Second, Hitpoints, Range, Damage Type, and Targets.": "Tapping this icon, which is displayed only while an upgrade is in progress, instantly finishes that upgrade at the cost of one Book of Building . This icon is only shown if you have at least one Book of Building."
      },
      {
        "": "",
        "Tapping this icon displays information about the Cannon, such as Level, Damage Per Second, Hitpoints, Range, Damage Type, and Targets.": "Tapping this icon, which is displayed only while an upgrade is in progress, instantly finishes that upgrade at the cost of one Book of Everything . This icon is only shown if you have at least one Book of Everything but do not have a Book of Building."
      },
      {
        "": "",
        "Tapping this icon displays information about the Cannon, such as Level, Damage Per Second, Hitpoints, Range, Damage Type, and Targets.": "Tapping this icon, which is displayed only while an upgrade is in progress, gives the player the option to assign a Builder's Apprentice to that Building. This icon only is only shown if you have unlocked Builder's Apprentice for 500 Gems ."
      },
      {
        "": "",
        "Tapping this icon displays information about the Cannon, such as Level, Damage Per Second, Hitpoints, Range, Damage Type, and Targets.": "Tapping this icon, which is displayed only while an upgrade is in progress, boosts all your Builders for 1 hour by a factor of ten, at the cost of one Builder Potion . This icon is only shown if you have at least one Builder Potion."
      },
      {
        "": "",
        "Tapping this icon displays information about the Cannon, such as Level, Damage Per Second, Hitpoints, Range, Damage Type, and Targets.": "Tapping this icon, which is displayed only while an upgrade is in progress, cancels the current upgrade and refunds half of the upgrade cost."
      },
      {
        "": "",
        "Tapping this icon displays information about the Cannon, such as Level, Damage Per Second, Hitpoints, Range, Damage Type, and Targets.": "Tapping this icon gears up the Cannon, if you have upgraded it enough to do so, have enough resources and a free Master Builder . If any Cannon is already geared up, this icon will not appear."
      },
      {
        "": "",
        "Tapping this icon displays information about the Cannon, such as Level, Damage Per Second, Hitpoints, Range, Damage Type, and Targets.": "This icon informs you that the Cannon cannot be geared up because it is insufficiently upgraded. Tapping this icon will tell you the required level to gear up this Cannon. If any Cannon is already geared up, this icon will not appear."
      },
      {
        "": "",
        "Tapping this icon displays information about the Cannon, such as Level, Damage Per Second, Hitpoints, Range, Damage Type, and Targets.": "This icon indicates that the Cannon is currently set to Normal mode, to attack units in the usual manner. Tapping this icon switches the Cannon to Burst mode. This icon only appears when the Cannon is geared up, and is in Normal mode."
      },
      {
        "": "",
        "Tapping this icon displays information about the Cannon, such as Level, Damage Per Second, Hitpoints, Range, Damage Type, and Targets.": "This icon indicates that the Cannon is currently set to Burst mode, to attack units with burst shots. Tapping this icon switches the Cannon to Normal mode. This icon only appears when the Cannon is geared up, and is in Burst mode."
      }
    ],
    [
      {
        "Date": "August 2, 2012",
        "Type": "The Cannon was present in the original release of the game, with 10 levels and four of them to build. At level 2, the whole Cannon is bigger and the base receives a wooden stabilizer tied to the legs with ropes. At level 3, the wood of rotational mount is now one whole piece instead of multiple wooden planks. The base itself rotates 45 degrees and the leg stabilizer becomes stouter. At level 4, the barrel is bigger and receives two decorative latitudinal ridges, one midway along the barrel and one at the rear. The platform's leg stabilizer is removed in favor of a larger and stouter main support platform with the rotational mount is fitted inside and has shorter legs. At level 5, the circular metal plate becomes bigger and the wooden legs are replaced with metal ones with a rivet. At level 6, the wood of rotational mount is replaced with metal. The base receives riveted metal plates on the sides of the platform to anchor the barrel more firmly to the rotational mount. At level 7, the barrel's decorative center ridges are thicker and trimmed to be more pointed, one more is added around the muzzle, and the middle is made of gold. The wooden base is discarded for a bigger white stone platform with four short gold-trimmed wooden legs. At level 8, the rear decorative ridge also becomes gold and the rotational mount is raised. A pair of gold plate is added to the right edge of the platform and its opposing side. At level 9, the muzzle decorative ridge also becomes gold and the bottom rotational mount has a straight edge. There are two additional gold plates perpendicular to the first pair and they are all wider, the side of them also receive a steel bolt with a gold top."
      },
